{
  "_comment": "Gaming Controller source, 8BITDO pad (wireless) -> Roomba target. Named after the CONTROLLER, like gamepad/dreamcast.json. Pair on macOS in B MODE (Start+B, D-input): in B mode this pad reports the same indices the Dreamcast pad does for the buttons below. Do NOT pair in X mode -- XInput renumbers everything (2=X,3=Y,dpad 12-15) and none of these keys would match. CONFIRMED indices: buttons 0=A,1=B,3=X,4=Y,11=Start; axis0=left stick X, axis2=left trigger, axis5=right trigger, axis9=dpad(unconfirmed values). Triggers are BUTTONS for forward/back: axis5(+)=drive-forward, axis2(+)=drive-back; turn-left/right uses axis0 sign. NOT YET CONFIRMED, so they appear on the pad and in `colors` but have NO BTN*/AXIS* entries in `actions` and drive nothing: L2, R2, SELECT, LS/RS (stick clicks), STAR, HEART, and the RIGHT STICK axes. Read their real indices off the Gaming Controller inspector and add them -- do not guess, D-input numbering varies by model and the right stick often collides with the trigger axes. Star/Heart frequently do not report at all in D-input.",
